var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"location":"heatmap_graphs.html#Heatmap-Graphs","page":"Heatmap Graphs","title":"Heatmap Graphs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"heatmap_graphs.html#Index","page":"Heatmap Graphs","title":"Index","text":"Pages = [\"heatmap_graphs.md\"]","category":"section"},{"location":"heatmap_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.HeatmapGraphs","page":"Heatmap Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.HeatmapGraphs","text":"Heatmap graphs of a metacells repository.\n\nA graph function fills in the data the graph is about, and nothing else. In particular it does not group the columns and does not annotate them. The caller says how, in a second call, so that any property can group or annotate:\n\ngraph = genes_heatmap_graph(daf; genes = get_skeleton_gene_indices(daf))\nfill_type!(columns_annotations_colors_vector_fields(graph, add_columns_annotation!(graph)), daf)\nfill_global_flow_order!(columns_groups_vector_data_fields(graph), daf)\nfill_block!(columns_subgroups_vector_data_fields(graph), daf)\n\nGrouping a level constrains the clustering to it and puts a gap between the groups. Naming both levels nests them: the blocks are grouped inside the types, which is how they nest. A level given numbers is laid out in the order of these numbers, and a level given names is laid out by the clustering.\n\nThe second call must name the same axis as the first. It needn't name the entries, since it fills the entries the graph was named after.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"heatmap_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.HeatmapGraphs.genes_heatmap_graph","page":"Heatmap Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.HeatmapGraphs.genes_heatmap_graph","text":"genes_heatmap_graph(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    genes::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    rows_axis_title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"Genes\",\n    columns_axis_title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"$(uppercasefirst(axis))s\",\n    max_fold::Real = 3.0,\n)::HeatmapGraph\n\nThe expression of the genes in each of the entries of the axis, as the fold factor of the gene from its median across the entries.\n\nThe genes are the rows and the entries are the columns; both are clustered. Pick the genes with a data source such as get_top_marker_gene_indices or get_skeleton_gene_indices, and name them in the rows_axis_title.\n\nThere are too many columns to label, so they are named in the hover of each cell instead. The rows are labelled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Data-Sources","page":"Data Sources","title":"Data Sources","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Generic","page":"Data Sources","title":"Generic","text":"These fill the data half of any role from a daf query. A specific data source uses them under the hood and adds only how to show the result. They hand the data to the generic puts of SomeGraphs.Sources.","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Axis-Names","page":"Data Sources","title":"Axis Names","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Axis-Vectors","page":"Data Sources","title":"Axis Vectors","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Frame-Columns","page":"Data Sources","title":"Frame Columns","text":"Some graphs show a report computed by Metacells, which is a DataFrame rather than a property of a daf repository. These fetch from a frame instead, and hand the result to the same put_ functions.","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Module-Regulators","page":"Data Sources","title":"Module Regulators","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Axes-Names","page":"Data Sources","title":"Axes Names","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Axes-Matrices","page":"Data Sources","title":"Axes Matrices","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Display-Buckets","page":"Data Sources","title":"Display Buckets","text":"Properties fall into a few buckets by how they are shown. Each bucket has one configuration function, and the data source of each property uses the function of its bucket.\n\nMost buckets also have generic data sources, taking the name of a property: a get, which fetches it, a fill, which fetches and shows it, and a put, which shows values already fetched. The data sources of the stored properties of each bucket (e.g. fill_n_cells!) are generated from a table. Each fetches with its own get, and shows the values with the put of its bucket.","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Expression","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Expression","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Expression-Vectors","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Expression Vectors","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Expression-Matrices","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Expression Matrices","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Fold-Matrices","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Fold Matrices","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Correlations","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Correlations","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Correlation-Changes","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Correlation Changes","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#UMAP-Coordinates","page":"Data Sources","title":"UMAP Coordinates","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Selection","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Selection","text":"These pick which genes a graph shows, and return indices to pass as the genes of another data source.","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Counts","page":"Data Sources","title":"Counts","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Total-UMIs","page":"Data Sources","title":"Total UMIs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Cells-and-Metacells","page":"Data Sources","title":"Cells and Metacells","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Means","page":"Data Sources","title":"Means","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Blocks","page":"Data Sources","title":"Blocks","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Global-Flow-Order","page":"Data Sources","title":"Global Flow Order","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Types","page":"Data Sources","title":"Types","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Gene-Flags","page":"Data Sources","title":"Gene Flags","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Low-Level-Functions","page":"Data Sources","title":"Low Level Functions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#Index","page":"Data Sources","title":"Index","text":"Pages = [\"data_sources.md\"]","category":"section"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources","text":"Data sources for the graphs of a metacells repository.\n\nA data source is a function extracting data from Daf metacells repositories and inserting it into a SomeGraphs graph. This uses the data source views (e.g. VectorDataFields, MatrixDataFields) provided for this purpose. These allow using the data for any graph role (coordinates, bar sizes, colors, annotations, etc.).\n\nA data source view has two halves: the data (what to show) and the configuration (how to show it). Each half is written the same way, by a get_ which fetches the data from daf and a put_ which writes the data into a graph, with a fill_ function that composes them:\n\nfunction takes does\nget_<something>_vector, ..._matrix daf and what to query returns the data\nput_<something>_data! sinks, the data writes the data fields to the graph\nfill_<something>_data! sinks, daf, what to query get_ then put_\nget_<something>_colors, ... daf and what to query returns what the configuration needs\nput_<something>_configuration! sinks, how to show it writes the configuration fields to the graph\nfill_<something>_configuration! sinks, daf, how to show it get_ (if needed) then put_\nfill_<something>! sinks, daf, everything composes whichever of the above exist\n\nIn most cases there's no need for getting data from daf for the configuration. In this case there's only a put function; there's no get and no need for a fill function.\n\nGeneric functions (e.g., axis_names, axis_vector, axes_matrix) only deal with data so have no configuration variants and no overall fill wrapper. Specific data (e.g., gene_expression, type) use these under the hood but add specific configuration for how to display the data in the graph.\n\nA get_ and a fill_ are named after where the data comes from, so a generic one says which daf axes it queries (axis_vector for one, axes_matrix for two). The generic put_ functions depend on nothing but the graph, so they are in SomeGraphs.Sources (e.g., put_vector_data!, put_matrix_names_data!). They are named after where the data goes, so they say which shape of sink they write, and the same one serves a DataFrame or any other source of a vector. A specific put_ here is named after its source instead, since there is only one shape it can take.\n\nThe fill and put functions take Sinks: a single graph struct, or a tuple or vector of them. This allows easily reusing the same data in multiple places in the graph (e.g., values, labels, hovers). A data function writes only the sinks which are a DataSink, and a configuration function only those which are a ConfigurationSink, so a mixed collection is fine and either may match nothing at all.\n\nA fill_ takes the entries of the axis to fill (and a matrix one also the genes or row_entries of its rows). When these aren't given, it uses the entries the sinks are already named after (see get_vector_names_data). Only when the sinks have no names does it use the whole axis. So when the first data source of a graph picks some entries, the rest follow it without being told which they are. Sinks named after different entries are an error.\n\nA put_ has a method per leaf it writes and one explicit no-op method for the leaves of its kind it ignores (e.g., a colors-only configuration ignores an axis). Its walking method takes everything else. A leaf covered by neither is a MethodError; in particular a matrix leaf handed to a vector put_, or the other way around.\n\nIn general the data and the configuration functions take different sets of parameters (e.g., axis for data and gene regularization for configuration of log scale). The title is a notable exception that gets passed to both sides, as it is used for computing hover values (data) and as an axis/legend title (configuration).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axis_names_data!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axis_names_data!","text":"fill_axis_names_data!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::Nothing\n\nName the entities of the sinks after each of the entries of the daf axis.\n\nThis fetches the names with get_axis_entries_vector, then hands them to put_vector_names_data!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_axis_entries_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_axis_entries_vector","text":"get_axis_entries_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}\n\nGet the name for each of the entries of the daf axis. If no entries are specified, returns the names of all the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axis_vector_data!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axis_vector_data!","text":"fill_axis_vector_data!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    query_suffix::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the result of the query @ axis query_suffix for each of the entries of the daf axis, and name the entities after the entries.\n\nThis fetches the data with get_axis_vector, then hands it to put_vector_data!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_axis_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_axis_vector","text":"get_axis_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    query_suffix::AbstractString,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Maybe{StorageScalarBase} = nothing,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:StorageScalarBase}\n\nGet the result of the query @ axis via query_suffix for each of the entries of the daf axis.\n\nThe via is a chain of axes to walk before asking anything, so that a property of something an entry belongs to can be asked for (e.g., the block of the metacell of each cell). An empty_value is what an entry whose chain breaks gets; a nothing leaves the query without a default, so such an entry is an error.\n\nThe query_suffix is whatever a vector query says at the end of that walk, e.g. \": block\" for a property or \":: linear_fraction @ gene = FOXA1\" for a slice of a matrix. It is written by the caller, so it is used as it is; everything else is escaped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_column_vector_data!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_column_vector_data!","text":"fill_column_vector_data!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    frame::DataFrame;\n    column::AbstractString,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the column of a frame, one value per row.\n\nThe entities are not named here, unlike fill_axis_vector_data!; a frame has no one column which identifies its rows, so say which one does with fill_column_names_data!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_column_names_data!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_column_names_data!","text":"fill_column_names_data!(sinks::VectorDataSinks, frame::DataFrame; column::AbstractString)::Nothing\n\nName the entities of the sinks after the column of a frame, one name per row.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_column_boolean_annotation!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_column_boolean_annotation!","text":"fill_column_boolean_annotation!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    frame::DataFrame;\n    column::AbstractString,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = column,\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the Boolean column of a frame, shown as true in black and false in light grey. The DataFrame twin of fill_boolean!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_column_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_column_vector","text":"get_column_vector(frame::DataFrame; column::AbstractString)::AbstractVector{<:StorageScalarBase}\n\nGet the column of a frame, one value per row. This is the DataFrame twin of get_axis_vector, for the graphs whose data is a report computed by Metacells rather than a property of a daf repository.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_module_regulators_hovers!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_module_regulators_hovers!","text":"fill_module_regulators_hovers!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    frame::DataFrame;\n    prefix::AbstractString,\n    side_name::AbstractString,\n    regulators_count::Integer,\n)::Nothing\n\nAdd a hover per row of a gene report frame to the sinks, saying which regulators the gene is in a module with in the base blocks of one side. The lines carry their own labels, so nothing is prefixed to them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_module_regulators_hovers","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_module_regulators_hovers","text":"get_module_regulators_hovers(\n    frame::DataFrame;\n    prefix::AbstractString,\n    side_name::AbstractString,\n    regulators_count::Integer,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}\n\nGet a hover per row of a gene report frame, saying how often the gene is in no module at all in the base blocks of one side, and which regulators it is most often in a module with there. The prefix picks that side's columns (imp or deg), and the side_name names it in the text.\n\nThe report pads a side which gives a gene fewer regulators than the regulators_count asked for with empty names, which are the regulators there is nothing to say about, and which are left out.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axes_names_data!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axes_names_data!","text":"fill_axes_names_data!(\n    sinks::MatrixDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    rows_axis::AbstractString,\n    columns_axis::AbstractString,\n    row_entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    column_entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::Nothing\n\nName the rows of the sinks after the row_entries of the daf rows_axis, and their columns after the column_entries of its columns_axis.\n\nThis fetches the names with get_axis_entries_vector, then hands them to put_matrix_names_data!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axes_matrix_data!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_axes_matrix_data!","text":"fill_axes_matrix_data!(\n    sinks::MatrixDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    rows_axis::AbstractString,\n    columns_axis::AbstractString,\n    query_suffix::AbstractString,\n    row_entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    column_entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the result of the query @ rows_axis @ columns_axis query_suffix, and name the rows and the columns. The matrix twin of fill_axis_vector_data!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_axes_matrix","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_axes_matrix","text":"get_axes_matrix(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    rows_axis::AbstractString,\n    columns_axis::AbstractString,\n    query_suffix::AbstractString,\n    row_entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    column_entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractMatrix{<:StorageScalarBase}\n\nGet the result of the query @ rows_axis @ columns_axis query_suffix for each of the row_entries and column_entries of the two daf axes. The matrix twin of get_axis_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_size_configuration!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_size_configuration!","text":"put_size_configuration!(\n    sinks::Sinks;\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nShow a size (a count) on a log scale of the log_base, regularized by 1, in the YlOrRd color scale, named by the title. This is how every count-like quantity is shown: how many cells, how many metacells, how many UMIs, and the means of these. They all span orders of magnitude, which is what the log scale is for. The regularization gives a zero count, which is rare, a place on the scale.\n\nThe color scale follows the range of the data. It runs from yellow through orange to red, so even the smallest count is visible. A scale which starts at white would lose it against the background.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_size_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_size_vector","text":"get_size_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n)::AbstractVector{<:Real}\n\nGet the size (count) property of each of the entries of the daf axis. By default this is the direct property of the axis entries. However, by specifying via, it is possible to access indirect sizes (e.g., the total UMIs of the block of the metacell of each cell).\n\nAn entry whose via chain breaks gets the empty_value, which is a count like any other, so the log scale has something to work with.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_size!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_size!","text":"fill_size!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = property,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the size (count) property of each of the entries of the daf axis (see get_size_vector), shown by put_size_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_size_values!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_size_values!","text":"put_size_values!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader,\n    value_per_entry::AbstractVector{<:Real};\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nPut the size (count) value_per_entry of each of the entries of the daf axis into the sinks, shown by put_size_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries. Every size data source ends with this.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_expression_level_configuration!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_expression_level_configuration!","text":"put_expression_level_configuration!(\n    sinks::Sinks;\n    gene_fraction_regularization::Real = 1.0e-5,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"fraction\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log2Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nShow an expression level (the fraction of the UMIs of a gene, or of a gene module) on a log scale of the log_base, regularized by gene_fraction_regularization, named by the title. The expression levels themselves are put in by put_vector_data! or put_matrix_data!.\n\nAs colors, the expression levels are shown in the WtYlOrRdDm color scale, which starts at zero. Zero expression is common, and is white, so any expression above it shows a color.\n\nThe show_legend applies where the expression levels are the colors. An axis is read off its own ticks and ignores it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.GENE_FRACTION_REGULARIZATION_FOR_GRAPHS","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.GENE_FRACTION_REGULARIZATION_FOR_GRAPHS","text":"The regularization added to a gene fraction before taking its log.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"constant"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_fold_configuration!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_fold_configuration!","text":"put_fold_configuration!(\n    sinks::Sinks;\n    max_fold::Real = MAX_FOLD_FOR_GRAPHS,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"fold from median\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nShow a fold (the log base 2 of a ratio, e.g. of a gene's expression to its median) in the range -max_fold (blue) to 0 (white) to +max_fold (red), named by the title, and include it in the legend if show_legend. The folds themselves are put in by put_vector_data! or put_matrix_data!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.MAX_FOLD_FOR_GRAPHS","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.MAX_FOLD_FOR_GRAPHS","text":"The extreme of the color scale of the log-base-2 fold factors between gene expression and median gene expression.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"constant"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_correlation_configuration!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_correlation_configuration!","text":"put_correlation_configuration!(\n    sinks::Sinks,\n    values::AbstractArray{<:Real};\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"correlation\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nShow a correlation (or a difference of correlations) on a linear scale, named by the title. The values are the ones put in by put_vector_data! or put_matrix_data!, and the colors follow their range.\n\nAs colors, zero is white, negative values go towards blue and positive values towards red, each side as far as the values go. The range always includes zero, even when all the values are positive (or all negative), so white always means no correlation. Unlike a fold, the range need not be symmetric, since most correlations are positive. If all the values are zero, the range is -1 to 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_vector","text":"get_correlation_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n)::AbstractVector{<:Real}\n\nGet the correlation property of each of the entries of the daf axis. By specifying via, it is possible to access an indirect correlation. An entry whose via chain breaks gets the empty_value, which by default means no correlation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation!","text":"fill_correlation!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = property,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the correlation property of each of the entries of the daf axis (see get_correlation_vector), shown by put_correlation_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_correlation_values!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_correlation_values!","text":"put_correlation_values!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader,\n    value_per_entry::AbstractVector{<:Real};\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nPut the correlation value_per_entry of each of the entries of the daf axis into the sinks, shown by put_correlation_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries. Every correlation data source ends with this.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_boolean_configuration!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_boolean_configuration!","text":"put_boolean_configuration!(\n    sinks::Sinks;\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nShow Boolean string values: true in black and false in light grey, named by the title. The values themselves are put in by put_vector_data!.\n\nBlack against light grey has only two values and is named by its title, so show_legend is off.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_boolean_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_boolean_vector","text":"get_boolean_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}\n\nGet the Boolean property of each of the entries of the daf axis, as the strings \"true\" and \"false\". Coloring by a Boolean is coloring by two categories, and a categorical palette is keyed by strings. By specifying via, it is possible to access an indirect property (e.g., whether the anchor gene of each module is a marker). An entry whose via chain breaks gets the empty_value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_boolean!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_boolean!","text":"fill_boolean!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = property,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the Boolean property of each of the entries of the daf axis (see get_boolean_vector), shown by put_boolean_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_boolean_values!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_boolean_values!","text":"put_boolean_values!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader,\n    value_per_entry::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString};\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nPut the Boolean string value_per_entry of each of the entries of the daf axis into the sinks, shown by put_boolean_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries. Every Boolean data source ends with this.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_category_configuration!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_category_configuration!","text":"put_category_configuration!(\n    sinks::Sinks,\n    color_per_value::CategoricalColors;\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nShow the values of a category (e.g. types or blocks) of the sinks using the color_per_value palette, named by the title. The values themselves are put in by put_vector_data!.\n\nThe palette is required, and covers every value, including the empty one of entries with no value. Where it comes from is up to the data source. For example, get_category_colors reads the colors given by the repository, or computes them.\n\nA color says nothing without a legend to read it by, so show_legend is on. Turn it off for a category with too many values to list, or for an annotation of a graph whose colors already name the same values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_category_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_category_vector","text":"get_category_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}\n\nGet the category property (e.g. the type) of each of the entries of the daf axis. By default this is the direct property of the axis entries. However, by specifying via, it is possible to access indirect values (e.g., the type of the block of the metacell of each cell). An entry whose via chain breaks gets the empty_value, which names no value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_category!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_category!","text":"fill_category!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    property::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = property,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n    colors_axis::AbstractString = property,\n    empty_color::Maybe{AbstractString} = EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the category property of each of the entries of the daf axis (see get_category_vector), shown by put_category_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries. The palette covers the colors_axis (see get_category_colors).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_category_values!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_category_values!","text":"put_category_values!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader,\n    value_per_entry::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString};\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n    colors_axis::AbstractString,\n    empty_color::Maybe{AbstractString} = EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nPut the category value_per_entry of each of the entries of the daf axis into the sinks, shown by put_category_configuration! using the palette of the colors_axis (see get_category_colors), and name the entities after the entries. Every category data source ends with this.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_category_colors","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_category_colors","text":"get_category_colors(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n    empty_color::Maybe{AbstractString} = EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR,\n)::OrderedDict{AbstractString, AbstractString}\n\nGet the palette mapping each entry of the daf axis of a category (e.g. the types or the blocks) to its color, with an additional empty_color for the empty_value of entries with no value. If the axis has a color vector (as the types usually do), the palette uses it, in the order of the axis. Otherwise, the colors come from categorical_palette, which spreads the entries over the cyclical HSV palette. Either way, the palette covers all the entries of the axis, so each value has the same color in every graph, whichever entries the graph shows.\n\nA nothing empty_color leaves the empty_value out of the palette, which says you expect every entry to have a value. An entry which doesn't is then rejected, because its value isn't a key of the palette.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR","text":"The color to give to entities without any value of a category (an empty string), e.g. with no type or no block. A computed palette takes its colors from the HSV palette, which holds only fully saturated colors. The \"grey\" color isn't one of them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"constant"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_coordinates_configuration!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_coordinates_configuration!","text":"put_coordinates_configuration!(sinks::Sinks; title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing)::Nothing\n\nShow the coordinates of an embedding (e.g. a UMAP) without ticks or a grid, named by the title. Only which points are near which other points means anything, so the values themselves are not worth labelling.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_gene_expression!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_gene_expression!","text":"fill_gene_expression!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    gene::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    gene_fraction_regularization::Real = GENE_FRACTION_REGULARIZATION_FOR_GRAPHS,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"$(gene) fraction\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log2Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the gene expression level (linear fraction) per each of the entries of some daf axis, shown by put_expression_level_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_gene_expression_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_gene_expression_vector","text":"get_gene_expression_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    gene::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the vector of the gene expression level (linear fraction) per each of the entries of some daf axis.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_genes_expression_matrix!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_genes_expression_matrix!","text":"fill_genes_expression_matrix!(\n    sinks::MatrixDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    genes::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    gene_fraction_regularization::Real = GENE_FRACTION_REGULARIZATION_FOR_GRAPHS,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"fraction\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log2Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the genes expression level (linear fraction) per each of the entries of some daf axis, shown by put_expression_level_configuration!, and name the rows and the columns. The genes are the rows and the entries are the columns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_genes_expression_matrix","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_genes_expression_matrix","text":"get_genes_expression_matrix(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    genes::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractMatrix{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the matrix of the genes expression level (linear fraction) per each of the entries of some daf axis. The genes are the rows and the entries are the columns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_genes_fold_matrix!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_genes_fold_matrix!","text":"fill_genes_fold_matrix!(\n    sinks::MatrixDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    genes::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    max_fold::Real = MAX_FOLD_FOR_GRAPHS,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"fold from median\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the genes fold (log base-2 minus the median) per each of the entries of some daf axis, shown in the range -max_fold (blue) to 0 (white) to +max_fold (red), and name the rows and the columns. The genes are the rows and the entries are the columns. This is based on the log_linear_fraction per gene per axis, which is already a log, so there's no regularization to apply here.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_genes_fold_matrix","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_genes_fold_matrix","text":"get_genes_fold_matrix(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    genes::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractMatrix{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the matrix of the genes fold (log base-2 minus the median) per each of the entries of some daf axis. The genes are the rows and the entries are the columns. This is based on the log_linear_fraction per gene per axis. The median of each gene is taken across the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_gene_correlation!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_gene_correlation!","text":"fill_gene_correlation!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    gene::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"base_block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"correlation\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the correlation of the gene per each of the entries of some daf axis, shown by put_correlation_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_gene_correlation_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_gene_correlation_vector","text":"get_gene_correlation_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    gene::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"base_block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the correlation of the gene between the cells of the neighborhood of each of the entries of some daf axis and their punctuated metacells. A zero is the gene saying nothing about that entry, rather than a correlation which happens to be zero.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation_between_cells_and_punctuated_metacells!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation_between_cells_and_punctuated_metacells!","text":"fill_correlation_between_cells_and_punctuated_metacells!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"cells correlation\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe correlation of each gene between the cells and their punctuated metacells. This fetches it with get_correlation_between_cells_and_punctuated_metacells_vector, and shows it with put_correlation_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_between_cells_and_punctuated_metacells_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_between_cells_and_punctuated_metacells_vector","text":"get_correlation_between_cells_and_punctuated_metacells_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe correlation of each gene between the cells and their punctuated metacells. This is directed at get_correlation_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_punctuated_metacells!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_punctuated_metacells!","text":"fill_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_punctuated_metacells!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"projected cells correlation\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe correlation of each gene between the cells and their projected punctuated metacells. This fetches it with get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_punctuated_metacells_vector, and shows it with put_correlation_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_punctuated_metacells_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_punctuated_metacells_vector","text":"get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_punctuated_metacells_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe correlation of each gene between the cells and their projected punctuated metacells. This is directed at get_correlation_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_metacells!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_metacells!","text":"fill_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_metacells!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"projection correlation\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe correlation of each gene between the query cells and their projected atlas metacells. This fetches it with get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_metacells_vector, and shows it with put_correlation_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_metacells_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_metacells_vector","text":"get_correlation_between_cells_and_projected_metacells_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe correlation of each gene between the query cells and their projected atlas metacells. This is directed at get_correlation_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_gene_correlation_change!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_gene_correlation_change!","text":"fill_gene_correlation_change!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader,\n    base_daf::DafReader;\n    gene::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"base_block\",\n    base_axis::AbstractString = \"base_block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"correlation change\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with how much the correlation of the gene changed between the base_daf and the daf, per each of the entries, and name the entities after them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_gene_correlation_change_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_gene_correlation_change_vector","text":"get_gene_correlation_change_vector(\n    daf::DafReader,\n    base_daf::DafReader;\n    gene::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"base_block\",\n    base_axis::AbstractString = \"base_block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet how much the correlation of the gene changed between the base_daf and the daf, per each of the entries. A value above zero is an entry whose metacells describe the gene better than the base does.\n\nThe same entries are the axis of the daf and the base_axis of the base_daf. They must therefore list the same names in the same order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_umap!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_umap!","text":"fill_umap!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    coordinate::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"UMAP $(uppercase(coordinate))\",\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the UMAP coordinate per each of the entries of some daf axis, shown without ticks or a grid, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_umap_data!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.put_umap_data!","text":"put_umap_data!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    coordinate_per_entry::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat};\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n)::Nothing\n\nPut a UMAP coordinate_per_entry into the sinks, as the values of a role.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_umap_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_umap_vector","text":"get_umap_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    coordinate::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the vector of the UMAP coordinate per each of the entries of some daf axis.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_top_marker_gene_indices","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_top_marker_gene_indices","text":"get_top_marker_gene_indices(daf::DafReader; markers_count::Integer)::Vector{Int}\n\nGet the indices of the markers_count best marker genes of a daf repository, to pass as the genes of another data source.\n\nA rank of 1 is the gene which best distinguishes between the cell states, and a non-marker gene is ranked above any count that can be asked for, so this is simply the genes ranked that high; a repository with fewer markers than that gives all of them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_skeleton_gene_indices","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_skeleton_gene_indices","text":"get_skeleton_gene_indices(daf::DafReader)::Vector{Int}\n\nGet the indices of the skeleton genes of a daf repository, to pass as the genes of another data source.\n\nUnlike the markers these are not ranked, and there are few enough of them to show them all. They are the genes the blocks were computed from, so they show what the blocks were told apart by.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_total_UMIs!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_total_UMIs!","text":"fill_total_UMIs!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"total UMIs\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe total UMIs of each entry. This fetches it with get_total_UMIs_vector, and shows it with put_size_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_total_UMIs_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_total_UMIs_vector","text":"get_total_UMIs_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe total UMIs of each entry. This is directed at get_size_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_n_cells!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_n_cells!","text":"fill_n_cells!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"cells\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe number of cells of each entry. Both metacells and blocks have one. This fetches it with get_n_cells_vector, and shows it with put_size_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_n_cells_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_n_cells_vector","text":"get_n_cells_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe number of cells of each entry. Both metacells and blocks have one. This is directed at get_size_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_n_metacells!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_n_metacells!","text":"fill_n_metacells!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"metacells\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe number of metacells of each entry. Only blocks have one, so the default axis is the block. This fetches it with get_n_metacells_vector, and shows it with put_size_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_n_metacells_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_n_metacells_vector","text":"get_n_metacells_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Real = 1,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe number of metacells of each entry. Only blocks have one, so the default axis is the block. This is directed at get_size_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_mean_cells_per_metacell!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_mean_cells_per_metacell!","text":"fill_mean_cells_per_metacell!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"mean cells per metacell\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the mean number of cells per metacell of each of the entries of the daf axis, shown by put_size_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_mean_cells_per_metacell_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_mean_cells_per_metacell_vector","text":"get_mean_cells_per_metacell_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the mean number of cells per metacell of each of the entries of the daf axis, which is its number of cells divided by its number of metacells.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_mean_total_UMIs_per_metacell!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_mean_total_UMIs_per_metacell!","text":"fill_mean_total_UMIs_per_metacell!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"mean UMIs per metacell\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the mean total UMIs per metacell of each of the entries of the daf axis, shown by put_size_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_mean_total_UMIs_per_metacell_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_mean_total_UMIs_per_metacell_vector","text":"get_mean_total_UMIs_per_metacell_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the mean total UMIs per metacell of each of the entries of the daf axis, which is its total UMIs divided by its number of metacells.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_mean_total_UMIs_per_cell!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_mean_total_UMIs_per_cell!","text":"fill_mean_total_UMIs_per_cell!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"mean UMIs per cell\",\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n    log_base::LogBase = Log10Base,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the mean total UMIs per cell of each of the entries of the daf axis, shown by put_size_configuration!, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_mean_total_UMIs_per_cell_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_mean_total_UMIs_per_cell_vector","text":"get_mean_total_UMIs_per_cell_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGet the mean total UMIs per cell of each of the entries of the daf axis, which is its total UMIs divided by its number of cells. Both metacells and blocks have both.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_block!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_block!","text":"fill_block!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"block\",\n    colors_axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    empty_color::Maybe{AbstractString} = EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR,\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe block of each entry. Blocks are shown as a grouping of an axis, as colors, as a hover, or any of these. There are too many blocks for a legend to help, so show_legend is off. This fetches it with get_block_vector, and shows it with put_category_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_block_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_block_vector","text":"get_block_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe block of each entry. Blocks are shown as a grouping of an axis, as colors, as a hover, or any of these. There are too many blocks for a legend to help, so show_legend is off. This is directed at get_category_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_block_colors","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_block_colors","text":"get_block_colors(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n    empty_color::Maybe{AbstractString} = EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR,\n)::OrderedDict{AbstractString, AbstractString}\n\nThe palette of the block axis, which shows the block. This is directed at get_category_colors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_global_flow_order!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_global_flow_order!","text":"fill_global_flow_order!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    type_property::AbstractString = \"type\",\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = nothing,\n)::Nothing\n\nFill the sinks with the global flow order of the type of each of the entries of the daf axis, and name the entities after the entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_global_flow_order_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_global_flow_order_vector","text":"get_global_flow_order_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    type_property::AbstractString = \"type\",\n    empty_value::Real = 0,\n)::AbstractVector{<:Real}\n\nGet the global flow order of the type of each of the entries of the daf axis. An entry with no type gets the empty_value, so it forms a group of its own at that end of the order.\n\nThe order is a property of the type, so all the entries of a type get the same number. Grouping an axis by it therefore groups the entries by their type, and lays the groups out in the flow order, so that every graph shows the types in the same order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_type!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_type!","text":"fill_type!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"type\",\n    colors_axis::AbstractString = \"type\",\n    empty_color::Maybe{AbstractString} = EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR,\n    show_legend::Bool = true,\n)::Nothing\n\nThe type of each entry, shown in the color of each type. This fetches it with get_type_vector, and shows it with put_category_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_type_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_type_vector","text":"get_type_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n)::AbstractVector\n\nThe type of each entry, shown in the color of each type. This is directed at get_category_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_type_colors","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_type_colors","text":"get_type_colors(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    empty_value::AbstractString = \"\",\n    empty_color::Maybe{AbstractString} = EMPTY_CATEGORY_COLOR,\n)::OrderedDict{AbstractString, AbstractString}\n\nThe palette of the type axis, which shows the type. This is directed at get_category_colors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_lateral!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_lateral!","text":"fill_is_lateral!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"lateral\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is lateral. This fetches it with get_is_lateral_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_lateral_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_lateral_vector","text":"get_is_lateral_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is lateral. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_marker!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_marker!","text":"fill_is_marker!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"marker\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is a marker gene. This fetches it with get_is_marker_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_marker_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_marker_vector","text":"get_is_marker_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is a marker gene. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_transcription_factor!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_transcription_factor!","text":"fill_is_transcription_factor!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"transcription factor\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is a transcription factor (binds to DNA). This fetches it with get_is_transcription_factor_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_transcription_factor_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_transcription_factor_vector","text":"get_is_transcription_factor_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is a transcription factor (binds to DNA). This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_regulator!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_regulator!","text":"fill_is_regulator!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"regulator\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene regulates the expression of other genes. This fetches it with get_is_regulator_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_regulator_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_regulator_vector","text":"get_is_regulator_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene regulates the expression of other genes. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_forbidden!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_forbidden!","text":"fill_is_forbidden!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"forbidden\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is forbidden. This fetches it with get_is_forbidden_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_forbidden_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_forbidden_vector","text":"get_is_forbidden_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is forbidden. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_skeleton!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_skeleton!","text":"fill_is_skeleton!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"skeleton\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is a skeleton gene. This fetches it with get_is_skeleton_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_skeleton_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_skeleton_vector","text":"get_is_skeleton_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is a skeleton gene. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_correlated_with_skeleton!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_correlated_with_skeleton!","text":"fill_is_correlated_with_skeleton!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"correlated with skeleton\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is correlated with some skeleton gene. This fetches it with get_is_correlated_with_skeleton_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_correlated_with_skeleton_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_correlated_with_skeleton_vector","text":"get_is_correlated_with_skeleton_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is correlated with some skeleton gene. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_mitochondrial!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_mitochondrial!","text":"fill_is_mitochondrial!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"mitochondrial\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is mitochondrial. This fetches it with get_is_mitochondrial_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_mitochondrial_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_mitochondrial_vector","text":"get_is_mitochondrial_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is mitochondrial. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_ribosomal!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_ribosomal!","text":"fill_is_ribosomal!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"ribosomal\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is ribosomal. This fetches it with get_is_ribosomal_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_ribosomal_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_ribosomal_vector","text":"get_is_ribosomal_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is ribosomal. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_excluded!","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.fill_is_excluded!","text":"fill_is_excluded!(\n    sinks::VectorDataSinks,\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n    title::Maybe{AbstractString} = \"excluded\",\n    show_legend::Bool = false,\n)::Nothing\n\nWhether each gene is excluded. This fetches it with get_is_excluded_vector, and shows it with put_boolean_values!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_excluded_vector","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_is_excluded_vector","text":"get_is_excluded_vector(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"gene\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    via::Maybe{Union{Tuple{Vararg{AbstractString}}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}} = nothing,\n    empty_value::Bool = false,\n)::AbstractVector\n\nWhether each gene is excluded. This is directed at get_boolean_vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_vector_query","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_vector_query","text":"get_vector_query(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    query::AbstractString,\n    indices::Maybe{AbstractVector{<:Integer}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractVector{<:StorageScalarBase}\n\nExecute a vector query on a daf repository and optionally access specific indices in it. This always returns a dense vector. If indices are specified this returns a copy of the data, not a view.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"data_sources.html#MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_matrix_query","page":"Data Sources","title":"MetacellsGraphs.DataSources.get_matrix_query","text":"get_matrix_query(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    query::AbstractString,\n    row_indices::Maybe{AbstractVector{<:Integer}} = nothing,\n    column_indices::Maybe{AbstractVector{<:Integer}} = nothing,\n)::AbstractMatrix{<:StorageScalarBase}\n\nExecute a matrix query on a daf repository and optionally access specific row_indices and/or column_indices in it. This always returns a dense matrix. If indices are specified this returns a copy of the data, not a view.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bar_graphs.html#Bar-Graphs","page":"Bar Graphs","title":"Bar Graphs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"bar_graphs.html#Index","page":"Bar Graphs","title":"Index","text":"Pages = [\"bar_graphs.md\"]","category":"section"},{"location":"bar_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.BarGraphs","page":"Bar Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.BarGraphs","text":"Bar graphs of a metacells repository.\n\nUnlike the other graphs, a graph here picks its own bars, so there is nothing for a caller to fill in afterwards. It reads a report computed by Metacells, keeps the genes worth showing, and draws everything about them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"bar_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.BarGraphs.improved_genes_graph","page":"Bar Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.BarGraphs.improved_genes_graph","text":"improved_genes_graph(;\n    daf::DafReader,\n    base_daf::DafReader,\n    genes_count::Integer = 30,\n    regulators_count::Integer = 5,\n)::SeriesBarsGraph\n\nThe genes_count genes whose correlation with their cells the metacells improved in the most of the base neighborhoods, as a butterfly of the percentage of neighborhoods each degraded in (to the left) and improved in (to the right).\n\nEverything drawn here is a column of compute_gene_report, which is what says when a gene is improved or degraded in a base block and which regulators it moves with; the graph picks the genes worth showing and draws them. A gene which is not a marker is not in the report and is therefore not shown.\n\nThe hover of each bar says how often the gene is in no module at all in that side's base blocks, and which regulators_count regulators it is most often in a module with there - that is, what the sharpening moved the gene with, where the bars say only how often it moved it. Each wing asks about its own base blocks, so the two hovers of a gene name different regulators.\n\nLateral and regulator genes are shown like any other, and are marked as such in the annotations between the two sides. A lateral gene high in this graph is worth looking at: it is a gene the analysis was told to ignore, which the metacells nevertheless describe better than the base does.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bar_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.BarGraphs.degraded_genes_graph","page":"Bar Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.BarGraphs.degraded_genes_graph","text":"degraded_genes_graph(;\n    daf::DafReader,\n    base_daf::DafReader,\n    genes_count::Integer = 30,\n    regulators_count::Integer = 5,\n)::SeriesBarsGraph\n\nThe genes_count genes whose correlation with their cells the metacells degraded in the most of the base neighborhoods.\n\nThis is improved_genes_graph picking its genes by the other side, and reads the same way; the two graphs show the same two series and differ only in which of them decides what is worth showing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"index.html#MetacellsGraphs","page":"MetacellsGraphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"index.html#Index","page":"MetacellsGraphs","title":"Index","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"index.html#MetacellsGraphs","page":"MetacellsGraphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs","text":"Draw the figures worth looking at of a metacells repository.\n\nThis sits between SomeGraphs, which draws heatmaps, scatters, bars and distributions from arrays and knows nothing of metacells, and Metacells, which computes what a metacells repository holds and draws nothing. A figure here reads a repository through DataAxesFormats, names its properties as Metacells does, and draws with SomeGraphs.\n\nIt does the arithmetic a figure needs and keeps the result in the figure: means, quantiles, normalizations, a fold factor from a median, the order a clustered heatmap is drawn in. It also gathers across repositories, which is how a figure compares the rounds of sharpening. What it does not do is produce data the repository should have held - if a number is worth storing, it belongs in a computation in Metacells, and nothing here writes to a repository.\n\nThe figures are meant to be asked for from a notebook: a call takes a repository and a few names and returns a figure, writes no files, and needs no output directory.\n\nThe included modules are:\n\n(Image: )\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"scatter_graphs.html#Scatter-Graphs","page":"Scatter Graphs","title":"Scatter Graphs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"scatter_graphs.html#Index","page":"Scatter Graphs","title":"Index","text":"Pages = [\"scatter_graphs.md\"]","category":"section"},{"location":"scatter_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs","page":"Scatter Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs","text":"Scatter graphs of a metacells repository.\n\nA graph function fills in the data the graph is about, and nothing else. In particular it does not color the points. The caller says how to color them in a second call, so that any property can be the color:\n\ngraph = umap_graph(daf)\nfill_type!(points_colors_vector_fields(graph), daf)\n\nThe second call must name the same axis as the first. It needn't name the entries, since it fills the entries the graph was named after. The same goes for the sizes of the points, and for anything else the graph leaves empty.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"scatter_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs.gene_gene_graph","page":"Scatter Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs.gene_gene_graph","text":"gene_gene_graph(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    x_gene::AbstractString,\n    y_gene::AbstractString,\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    gene_fraction_regularization::Real = 1.0e-5,\n)::PointsGraph\n\nThe expression of x_gene against y_gene, a point per each of the entries of the axis, on log scale.\n\nThe axis can be any axis which has a linear_fraction per gene, typically metacell or block. A block is coarser, so the same pair of genes shows fewer points and less scatter.\n\nThe hover of each point names its entry and gives both fractions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"scatter_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs.umap_graph","page":"Scatter Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs.umap_graph","text":"umap_graph(\n    daf::DafReader;\n    axis::AbstractString = \"metacell\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n)::PointsGraph\n\nThe 2D UMAP embedding, a point per each of the entries of the axis.\n\nThe axis can be any axis which has UMAP coordinates, typically metacell or block. A block is placed at the mean position of its metacells, so the same embedding shows fewer points closer to its center.\n\nThe coordinates are the arbitrary output of the UMAP projection, so the axes are drawn without ticks or a grid. Only which points are near which other points means anything.\n\nThe hover of each point names its entry and gives its coordinates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"scatter_graphs.html#MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs.gene_base_delta_correlations_graph","page":"Scatter Graphs","title":"MetacellsGraphs.ScatterGraphs.gene_base_delta_correlations_graph","text":"gene_base_delta_correlations_graph(;\n    daf::DafReader,\n    base_daf::DafReader,\n    gene::AbstractString,\n    axis::AbstractString = \"base_block\",\n    base_axis::AbstractString = \"block\",\n    entries::Maybe{Union{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}} = nothing,\n    gene_fraction_regularization::Real = 1.0e-5,\n)::PointsGraph\n\nWhat the metacells did to one gene, a point per each of the entries: how much its correlation with the cells changed, against how much of the gene there is to say anything about.\n\nBoth repositories hold the correlations along the axis. The base_daf holds the expression along its base_axis instead, because what is a base block there is also a block. The two must list the same names in the same order.\n\nThe x axis is the gene's correlation between the cells of the entry's neighborhood and their punctuated metacells, minus what it is in the base_daf. A point right of zero is an entry whose metacells describe the gene better than the base does. The y axis is how much of the gene the entry expresses, on log scale, since moving the correlation of a gene which is barely there says less than moving one which is everywhere.\n\nOnly the entries whose base correlation is not zero are shown. A zero there is what a gene saying nothing about an entry looks like, rather than a correlation which happens to be zero. A gene which says nothing about any entry has nothing to show and is an error rather than an empty graph. The hidden entries stay in the data, masked, and do not affect the ranges of the axes.\n\nThe hover of each point names its entry and gives both correlations, the change between them, and the fraction of the gene.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"}]
}
